🟠 postgres in shop (prod-eu-1) keeps running out of memory because its memory limit is too low for normal use. It was killed within 10 seconds of starting. The error mentions it. services api, gateway and postgres can't serve traffic. Its containers have no memory limit, so nothing stopped them before the node ran short. It runs a single replica, so this is downtime, not degradation. To read the output of the last crash, run kubectl logs postgres-1ff9723b-a -c app -n shop --previous
Chain: postgres (10:09) → api (10:10) → gateway (10:10) → web (10:10). Beyond that, service web (10:10) also fails; kwatch follows a chain at most 3 steps, so it is reported on its own.
